**Goal:** Find missing access control, owner bypasses, and unprotected token issuance.

**Technique:**
Scan the ABI for STATE-MUTATING functions whose names suggest privileged operations (typical name patterns: set*, change*, update*, upgrade*, transferOwnership*, renounce*, pause*, unpause*, emergency*, drain*, rescue*, sweep*, withdraw*, mint*, burn*, initialize*, init* — but use whatever this ABI actually has). Call ALL such functions from attacker_address (an unprivileged caller) — if any succeeds without reverting on auth, that's an access-control bug. Three high-yield sub-cases to ALWAYS try:
